\[
\kappa(C_1)=\max(p,q),\qquad
\kappa(C_r)=p+q\ (r\geq2).
\]

The proof survives. Classification: **CORRECT BUT MINOR; exact priority uncertain**. Rectangle marginals give rank-one recovery; parity gives the lower bounds. The phenomenon is not uniquely GF(2). Most other Q_k theorems are standard Fourier/marginal, trade, or Chow consequences.

